#: src/3808-register-tool.md:1
msgid "Feature Name: `register_tool`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3808-register-tool.md:2
msgid "Start Date: 2025-03-22"
msgstr ""

#: src/3808-register-tool.md:3
msgid "RFC PR: [\\#3803](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3808)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3808-register-tool.md:4
msgid ""
"Rust Issue: [rust-lang/rust#66079](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"issues/66079)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3808-register-tool.md:6
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: src/3808-register-tool.md:9
msgid "This RFC adds three new attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3808-register-tool.md:10
msgid ""
"`#![register_lint_tool(tool_name)]` allows controlling namespaced lints with "
"`#[warn(tool_name::lint_name)]`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3808-register-tool.md:11
msgid ""
"`#![register_attribute_tool(tool_name)]` allows using tool names in [inert "
"attributes](https://rustc-dev-guide.rust-lang.org/attributes."
"html#builtininert-attributes) with `#[tool_name::"
"attribute_name(token_tree)]`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3808-register-tool.md:12
msgid ""
"`#![register_tool(tool_name)]` is an alias for `#!"
"[register_lint_tool(tool_name)] #![register_attribute_tool(tool_name)]`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3808-register-tool.md:14
msgid ""
"Note that this does not add any new functionality into the compiler; it only "
"relaxes the current restrictions. While `rustc` verifies that tool "
"attributes and lints are syntactically valid and do not cause ambiguity "
"during name resolution, it does no extra processing."
msgstr ""

#: src/3808-register-tool.md:16
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3808-register-tool.md:19
msgid ""
"There are [several tools predefined in the tool namespace](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/nightly/reference/attributes.html#tool-attributes). These tools are "
"hard-coded, and cannot be extended with user-defined tools. There are many "
"external programs that would benefit from being able to annotate specific "
"portions of a crate or register custom lints without the compiler raising an "
"error."
msgstr ""

